    "definitions": {
      "short": "something said",
      "usage": "answer, × appointed unto him, saying, speech, word.",
      "full": "H561. emer [ אִמְרָה ] noun feminine utterance, speech, word (in poetry, mostly singular collective, compare plural verb Psa 119:103 , but here read probably Pluraln. compare ᵐ5 Ol Hi De Che) — construct אִמְרַת Isa 5:24 +; אִמְרָתִי Gen 4:23 + etc.; Plural absolute אֲמָרוֺת Psa 12:7 ; construct אִמֲרוֺת ib.; — utterance, speech Gen 4:23 (song of Lamech, || קוֺל ); so Isa 28:23 ; 32:9 ; Deut 32:2 (|| לֶקַח ), Psa 17:9 ; Isa 29:4 (twice in verse) (|| also דִּבֶּד ); especially saying(s), words(s) of ׳י (command & promise) Deut 33:9 (|| בְּרִית ); Isa 5:24 (|| תּוֺרָה ) 2Sam 22:31 = Psa 18:31 ; 12:7 ; 105:19 (|| דָּבָר ; esp 119:11 ; 119:38 ; 119:41 16 t.; 138:2 ; 147:15 (|| דָּבָר ), Prov 30:5 .",
